Derived from fermented corn starch, maize, or sugarcane (   density,    tensile strength,    flexural strength), neat PLA suffers from a low glass transition temperature (   of   ), slow crystallization kinetics, and strictly industrial compostability2. Unmodified PLA should be restricted to thin secondary components or paired with natural thermal and mechanical insulators17. For example, in pressed powder or solid lip compacts, 3D Cork pairs a molded PLA structural base and magnetic pan insert with an agglomerated cork lid colored with water-based pigments and bonded via bio-based adhesives; the entire assembly is engineered for tool-free manual disassembly so the consumer can separate the cork lid, PLA structure, and magnet at end-of-life32. Similarly, HNB Corporation utilizes    PLA handles paired with    corn-fiber bristles in eco-designed cosmetic brushes8. When PLA must be used in higher-stress structural applications, compounding it with    zeolite shifts its crystalline morphology from the   -phase to the more stable   -phase, elevating tensile strength from    to   33.
Molded Agricultural Pulp (Bamboo and Sugarcane Bagasse)
To achieve true backyard compostability for the disposable refill cartridge, non-wood agricultural by-products—specifically bamboo pulp and sugarcane bagasse—are blended into an aqueous slurry and thermoformed into rigid, paper-like cylinders or cups5. Commercialized in the Maya refillable lipstick series (adopted by Wild) and European deodorant refills (adopted by Fler), these agricultural fibers regenerate rapidly without forest clearing, carry a minimal carbon footprint, and disintegrate in ambient home soil without leaving microplastic residues5.


